A||||3||fieroman_5000||Cruise control????||||5||
Z||000000||fieroman_5000||10-26-2001||07:49 AM||||Does anyone know how to tell if you have cruise control by looking at the engine?<BR>I ask cause I have some wires snipped in the steering column...but everything works. I'm wondering if it previosly had cruise.<P>Thanx<BR>Fieroman <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||Leadfoot||10-26-2001||12:00 PM||||Welcome!  You can tell if had cruise by looking to see if there is a cable coming from the throttle body to the back left of the engine bay.  The cable should connect to a bulky cruise control solenoid.  Right below it there should be a vacuum canister (looks like a coffee can). ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fformula88||10-26-2001||12:15 PM||||I think the coffee can is on all Fieros (my dads non-cruise 87 coupe had one anyway).  But thats the location.  Above the canister is the cruise control workings.  The cable from the throttle will connect to a rubber diaphram that is roughly as big around as a softball.  This is all located at the top of the luggage compartment firewall, engine side, right next to the drivers side rear strut tower.  Can't miss it!||||reg||1
Z||000003||fieroman_5000||10-26-2001||05:40 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fformula88:<BR><B>Above the canister is the cruise control workings.  The cable from the throttle will connect to a rubber diaphram that is roughly as big around as a softball.  This is all located at the top of the luggage compartment firewall, engine side, right next to the drivers side rear strut tower.  Can't miss it!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Does the rubber diaphram move in and out?  is it kinda like putting a piece of plastic over a glass and pushing it in and out?<P>And yes I do have the 'coffee can' if that has any relevance.<P>Thanx<BR>Fieroman  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
